  "constitutional_laws": [
    "one physical hierarchy engine supports many independent logical taxonomy systems",
    "taxonomy depth is unbounded and depth labels are presentation vocabulary",
    "semantic identity is independent of label and tree placement",
    "taxonomy is tree_or_forest plus many_to_many target assignments plus explicit cross_taxonomy mappings",
    "tenant overlays and base placement changes may never create an effective hierarchy cycle",
    "classification never acquires target domain authority",
    "inherited global or pack trees are not copied per tenant; tenants persist deltas",
    "pack and template applicability is supplied by composition context; templates do not own semantics",
    "family_variant, offer composition, recipe_BOM, inventory and Finance remain separate from classification",
    "historical placement and provenance remain explainable from this checkpoint forward",
    "AI may consume or suggest semantics but governed authorities perform mutation"
  ],
